  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\qt0005_c1dbd72cdea3.png\"/><br/>\nIn the given circuit the sliding contact is pulled outwards such that electric current in the circuit changes at the rate of $8 \\mathrm{~A} / \\mathrm{s}$. At an instant when R is $12 \\Omega$, the value of the current in the circuit will be ______ A."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\varepsilon-\\frac{\\mathrm{LdI}}{\\mathrm{dt}}-\\mathrm{IR}=0 \\\\ & 12-3 \\times(-8)-\\mathrm{I} \\times 12=0 \\\\ & \\mathrm{I}=3\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}